.TH "PB-TUNNEL-POLICY-REVOKE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-policy-revoke - Revoke an on-demand port policy


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel policy revoke <policy> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Revoke an on-demand port policy

.PP
Revoke one exact on-demand port policy at its expected generation. Subsequent activations are denied; this does not delete unrelated tunnel routes.

.PP
An on-demand policy authorizes an exact machine port for private or team access. A policy does not publish a public URL or grant every port on the machine. Revocation fences subsequent activation.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected policy generation; omitted reads current state first

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for revoke

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel-policy(1)\fP
